# Pairs with EveryCommittedKeyReadable. A leaf that applies the commit terminal
# but leaves its materialised projection on the pre-saga value never makes the
# committed write readable, even though the saga terminates normally.
#
# Note this is deliberately NOT the "drop fairness" mutation: that would stall
# the saga and so would fire Termination too, which proves nothing about THIS
# property. Here every saga still terminates and the leads-to still fails,
# which is the distinction the two liveness properties are meant to draw.
MODULE: EveryCommittedKeyReadableStaleProjection
TARGET: EveryCommittedKeyReadable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: leaves the leaf projection on the pre-saga value after a commit terminal, so the write is never readable

--- FIND
ProjectedPrepared(t, k) == terminal[t][k] = "commit"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the projection switches on an ABORT terminal rather than a commit
\* one, so a committed key is never materialised at its post-saga value however
\* long a reader waits.
ProjectedPrepared(t, k) == terminal[t][k] = "abort"
--- END
